							</td>
							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=6.0">Blacklist</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=758.15#msg6833">Re:Vertigion and Hookin of &quot;Reckoning Force&quot;</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: April 07, 2004, 11:23:09 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Shakro link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6828 date=1081390428</div><div class="quote">…asshole-ness that unfortunately has become more and more common in EQ through the years. &nbsp;You don&#039;t have priority rights to <i>an entire level 20s zone</i> just because you&#039;ve got a high level character (who doesn&#039;t?) and, no, at no point does training someone else become ok just because you already killed them 2 or 3 times. &nbsp;If anything, in my eyes you become more and more of a jerk each time you do it.</div><br />Thank you for this bit of insight. &nbsp;Once again, I did not deliberately train them nor did I have any intention of killing them. &nbsp;Victim of circumstance comes to mind again. &nbsp;Already said my apologies (and truly meant them). &nbsp;I was, however, there first and thus had priorities to continue doing what I had been doing for three hours prior. &nbsp;It’s unfortunate that people expect you to stop what you’re doing because some newbie gets in the way … again … and again … and again. &nbsp;I offered rezes in sympathy. &nbsp;They must have been over looked.<br /><hr /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Shakro link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6828 date=1081390428</div><div class="quote">There&#039;s enough mobs in SolA to support half a dozen groups or more, so there&#039;s zero reason that two groups couldn&#039;t have shared it in peace.</div><br />In response to this: <div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Tlera link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6823 date=1081379189</div><div class="quote">Well I did try to work it out and Vert and Hook offered to get them set up in a camp with Exp that they would stay well away from. &nbsp;He also offered rezzes which I tried to pass on, but they didn&#039;t want to hear anything about it. &nbsp;</div> I agreed to let them set up camp and stay away. &nbsp;I was willing to share.<br /><hr /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Givins link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6826 date=1081384450</div><div class="quote">You&#039;re right man. &nbsp;What a bunch of idiots we were, trying to zone in to Sol A and try to CR while you&#039;re PLing. &nbsp;Stupid us. &nbsp;We had absolutely no business being there. &nbsp;Next time I see you in the zone, I&#039;ll be sure to zone out so you can have the zone to yourself.</div>Thank you for that kind offer, but it’s not necessary. &nbsp;Politeness goes a long way though …<br /><hr /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Givins link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6826 date=1081384450</div><div class="quote">…people are OOCing, ASKING that you stop just long enough for them to rezz and you refuse to comply, I cannot believe that you had any good intentions at all. &nbsp;And perhaps I missed it, but no rezzes were ever offered and no one was ever given a clicky.</div> I agreed to stop training actually. &nbsp;I’m sorry you took quite a bit of loss before you asked. &nbsp;I figured you would have asked sooner and made sure the situation was clear before you went back in to get corpses. &nbsp;Asking when Hookin has 30~ mobs on him doesn’t do you any good. &nbsp;We stopped the pulls, I’m sorry you got hit by the train that was compiled while you where asking. &nbsp;It would have made sense to make sure things were settled down before attempting another CR.<br /><br />Was I going to just go rez your people without making sure you didn’t have a cleric on the way? &nbsp;(Possibly zoning in at that time where his/her time would have been wasted by running out there to help you.) &nbsp;Nope. &nbsp;You must have missed the /tells from Tlera and both of my /ooc … that sucks. &nbsp;I’m sorry you missed the messages.<br /><hr /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Givins link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6826 date=1081384450</div><div class="quote"> &nbsp;Heh, my favorite line was when you answered our request to stop pulling for just a minute with an OOC in all caps: &nbsp;GET OUT OF OUR WAY and you proceeded to pull another train of 30+ goblins over 2 members of our party, insta killing them.</div>See above … once again, the train was already in progress. &nbsp;He was basically telling you to move it or lose it … here comes another one. &nbsp;Next time, I’ll have him type it slower so that you can get a grasp of what is going on. &nbsp;I realize with a lot going on at once, things can get confusing. &nbsp;Once again, sorry this happened to you.<br /><hr /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Tlera link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6823 date=1081379189</div><div class="quote">…the 3&#039;rd of 4&#039;th tell I got from them was that our guild sickens them.</div>Clearly you(Givins)/your people(Shakro) were completely, 100% doing the right/good-hearted/professional thing. &nbsp;Please ask for the log, Shakro. &nbsp;I know I missed some messages that I would like to review during our train pulling to our camp site.<br /><hr /><br />I’m not trying to battle, simply pointing out the facts. &nbsp;Once again, as I said in my previous post: <div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Vertigion link=board=6;threadid=758;start=0#msg6817 date=1081373350</div><div class="quote">I would like to take this last paragraph to formerly apologize in front of all of RN. &nbsp;I&#039;m truely sorry that you were a victim of circumstance. &nbsp;I&#039;m also truely sorry it wasn&#039;t handled better, by both ends.</div></td>
						</tr>
