							<td align="left" style="padding: 0 1ex;">
								6
							</td>
							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=6.0">Blacklist</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=758.15#msg6817">Re:Vertigion and Hookin of &quot;Reckoning Force&quot;</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: April 07, 2004, 05:29:10 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">WOOT! &nbsp;He posted!! &nbsp;You told Tlera you had log running ... please post it then, thanks.<br /><br />Ok, here&#039;s the deal ...<br />Yes, this is the original Vertigion and I was not farming plat, gawd. &nbsp;Definitely not ebayer, I&#039;ve been playing since Kunark and can think of plenty of better ways to get plat then SolA. &nbsp;I was PLing a bard (Tempeest) and pally (Hosyla) (Hosyla was 2-boxing his shaman (Koree-65)) friend of mine. &nbsp;They where level 20~ and it was awesomely quick experience for them. &nbsp;DS myself, run a train into the room near zone in that u can zone into SolB, back myself into a corner, let the bard AE song the masses and they beat themselves to death on my DS!<br /><br />Anyway, he and two of his friends ran right out front of our camp (just past the window) and made camp there. &nbsp;Of course, we&#039;ve been there for several hours with no one in the zone and haven&#039;t been calling train. &nbsp;Sure enough, one run, there&#039;s a monk there fighting something. &nbsp;I guess he failed to FD when the train came to him, but as you all know when you&#039;re fighting a mob, and more run past, they agro to you as well, and since all I was doing was standing next to them to agro, I had no &quot;real&quot; agro to keep them on me. &nbsp;Regardless, he died, I didn&#039;t notice, nothing was said that I remember. &nbsp;Apparently, he died 3 times like this and then his group died. &nbsp;Did I feel bad? &nbsp;Yah, it was my bad the first time. &nbsp;Maybe it was my fault the second. &nbsp;It was your fault the third and fourth for staying there. &nbsp;They where pissed and showing it in /ooc and demanded my Guild Leaders name (Hakamur) ... I gave them Lead Officers name (Tlera) since Hak wasn&#039;t on. &nbsp;Anyway, after some heated arguments in /ooc we continued training. &nbsp;They asked if they could please have time to cr and leave the zone since it was &quot;our zone&quot;. &nbsp;(No one said it was our zone, but we where there first and essentially had priority camp rights to the entire zone sine we where able to succesfully pull and kill the entire zone ... according to the un-written rules of camping.) &nbsp;And we let them have enough time to gather corpses and clear out.<br /><br />Of course, the enchanter banned Me (Druid) AND Hookin (Monk) from KEI from his enchanter. &nbsp;Of course, Hookin was heart-broken. &nbsp;I was a little upset that I would have to continue to log my friend&#039;s 65 enc account for VoQ. &nbsp;<br /><br />I also want to point out that I had a 58 cleric parked with us for rezes and offered to rez them once I found out they where dead (and the heated arguments ended) and I got no reply.<br /><br />They had a nice conversation with Tlera (I&#039;ll let him post the details if he wishes), and they where rude with him despite that Tlera was (and always is) as polite with people as possible. &nbsp;Of course, when he mentioned that I was petitioned and they would get me banned from the server, Tlera laughed, but &nbsp;... heck ... that&#039;s just funny since we all (least those of us whom aren&#039;t newbies) know how awesomely helpful GMs are with this kind of thing. &nbsp;And I was 100% within my rights since I was not deliberately training them, they were just the victims of circumstance.<br /><br />I would like to take this last paragraph to formerly apologize in front of all of RN. &nbsp;I&#039;m truely sorry that you were a victim of circumstance. &nbsp;I&#039;m also truely sorry it wasn&#039;t handled better, by both ends.<br /><br />Ok, I&#039;m over it ... ciao!</td>
						</tr>
